{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791796308,"nonce":"8vhzk0Ew5r2WIDbL3suiITFhkUo=","title":"Generic phi nodes keep unresolved types after specialization","message":"A generic enum payload extraction lowered through a switch uses a TypeVar(T) result phi. Monomorphizer::substitute_cfg substitutes instruction types but skips block.phi_nodes, leaving phi.ty as TypeVar(T) even though the register table and function return become F64.\n\nReproducer: haxe-conformance/regressions/GadtConstructorParameters.hx, extract\u003cT\u003e(Wrapped\u003cT\u003e):T called on Wrapped\u003cFloat\u003e. Native Haxe returns 2.5. The intermediate Rayzor source preserving constructor-local parameters reports: Verifier errors in extract__f64: result 0 has type i64, must match function signature of f64. Post-mono MIR still contains phi ?T.\n\nThe switch result also needs a generic default and its local binding must preserve a TypeVar register rather than erase it to I64 before specialization. The functional fixture covers Int, Float and String extraction along with reordered and nested constructor parameters.","files":null}]}